// Cycle of Life: Realistic Fauna - FotSA New Zealand flightless birds (Dinornithiformes Plus).
//
// The single strangest fauna in the pack: 42 species across ten families from a land that had no
// land mammals at all, so birds took every role. Nine moa, five kiwi, two adzebills, six waterfowl
// (including two flightless grazing geese the size of small sheep), eleven rails, the kakapo, an
// owlet-nightjar, and seven New Zealand wrens down to a six-gram rifleman.
//
// NEST AND EGG ENTITIES NEED NO HANDLING. Every family ships a nest -> egg -> bird chain, and the
// nest and egg entities carry the "nest" and "egg" entity tags, which the mod's own tag filter
// already drops as non-fauna (along with the moa carcass). That removes 169 of the 211 keys this
// mod would otherwise produce, leaving exactly the 42 adults tuned here. If a future version stops
// tagging them, they would need explicit exclusion or a chainSeed marker instead.
//
// WHAT IS INHERITED. Body weights are per-sex on the moa, kiwi and kakapo and are good - the moa
// dimorphism in particular is correct and remarkable, with Dinornis hens at 200 kg against 70 kg
// cocks. Diets are right where they are declared: the moa and kakapo browse Fruit/Grain/Vegetable,
// the rails are omnivores, and the wrens, kiwi, owlet-nightjar and adzebills are deliberately given
// NO plant diet, which correctly leaves them outside the forage model - they ate invertebrates.
// Group caps are sensible almost everywhere.
//
// WHAT IS CHANGED, and why:
//   * WREN WEIGHTS. The mod puts the wrens at 0.07-0.5 kg; the real birds are 6-50 grams, so every
//     one is roughly ten times too heavy. Corrected per species. They are not foragers, so this
//     mostly affects their satiation reserve and roaming, but it should still read true.
//   * THE TWO CNEMIORNIS GEESE get Vegetable/Grain and isForager. They were terrestrial grazing
//     geese - that is the whole point of them - and with no declared diet they would sit outside
//     the forage model entirely, which for a 15-18 kg grazer is the one thing it should be in.
//   * KAKAPO K 4 -> 1. Four per 0.173 km² is about 23 per km², far denser than kakapo ever were.
//
// LIFECYCLES are the bulk of this file, and New Zealand birds are extreme even by this pack's
// standards. Moa took about a decade to reach adult size - up to nine growth rings have been
// counted in their leg bones, exceptionally slow for any bird, and one of the reasons they could
// not absorb hunting. Kiwi incubate for 70-80 days, roughly the gestation of a similar-sized
// mammal, and lay an egg up to a fifth of the female's mass. Kakapo live 60-90 years, breed only
// when the rimu masts every two to four years, and males do not breed until their teens.
//
// A NOTE ON THAT SLOW MATURATION: it is expressed through low growthRate, NOT through
// lifecycle.maturityDays. Maturity is auto-discovered from the entity's own grow chain, and raising
// it to a literal ten years would mean birds that look fully grown are still counted as juveniles,
// so they would never breed and the population would collapse. The growth rate carries the meaning
// instead - moa and kakapo simply replace themselves very rarely.
//
// VERIFICATION STATUS: keys derived from the mod's own entity JSON, not read off a live roster -
// this mod is not installed on the pack author's server. A wrong key is inert (the entry is ignored
// and the animal keeps its auto-discovered values); `/col species` lists the authoritative keys.
{
